3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,57960,7141,4779,57960,19127,4779,323,57960,32214,3,387,2326,25941,1741,429,57960,7141,488,1124,19127,488,1124,32214,284,1124,2493,2418,220,1416,582,525,2661,429,57960,52591,1124,7141,1124,52591,1124,19127,284,1124,66,2388,1124,37018,35702,2493,15170,18,2137,3,1221,8253,57960,37018,35702,9407,1124,7141,1124,9407,1124,19127,15170,59,9407,1124,32214,92,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $\\alpha,$ $\\beta,$ and $\\gamma$ be three angles such that $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi.$  If we are given that $\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3},$ then determine $\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma}.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"084e62b600ab4e83258614478fb6a0dd769b3fe96e368eb1af1d447749ed3660"},"seconds":60.639986991882324,"seed":1028193855488935176,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we will use trigonometric identities and the given information step-by-step.\n\n1. **Given Information:**\n   - \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\)\n   - \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\)\n\n2. **Convert \\(\\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) to a simpler form:**\n   \\[\n   \\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3} = \\frac{1}{\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\n3. **Use the identity \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\gamma = \\pi - (\\alpha + \\beta)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Express \\(\\cos \\gamma\\) in terms of \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = \\cos(\\pi - (\\alpha + \\beta)) = -\\cos(\\alpha + \\beta)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Use the cosine addition formula:**\n   \\[\n   \\cos(\\alpha + \\beta) = \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\n   \\]\n   Thus,\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = -(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta) = \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta - \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n6. **Express \\(\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\\) in terms of \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = \\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n   Given \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n7. **Substitute \\(\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\\) back into the expression for \\(\\cos \\gamma\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta = \\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} - 1\\right) \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n8. **Calculate the coefficient:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} - 1 = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = \\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}\\right) \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n9. **Determine \\(\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma} = \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}\\right) \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta} = \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}\n   \\]\n\n10. **Rationalize the denominator:**\n    \\[\n    \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3} - 3} \\cdot \\frac{2\\sqrt{3} + 3}{2\\sqrt{3} + 3} = \\frac{3(2\\sqrt{3} + 3)}{(2\\sqrt{3})^2 - 3^2} = \\frac{3(2\\sqrt{3} + 3)}{12 - 9} = \\frac{3(2\\sqrt{3} + 3)}{3} = 2\\sqrt{3} + 3\n    \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\sqrt{3} + 3}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2\\sqrt{3} + 3}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we will use trigonometric identities and the given information step-by-step.\n\n1. **Given Information:**\n   - \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\)\n   - \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\)\n\n2. **Convert \\(\\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) to a simpler form:**\n   \\[\n   \\csc \\frac{\\pi}{3} = \\frac{1}{\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\n3. **Use the identity \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\gamma = \\pi - (\\alpha + \\beta)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Express \\(\\cos \\gamma\\) in terms of \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = \\cos(\\pi - (\\alpha + \\beta)) = -\\cos(\\alpha + \\beta)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Use the cosine addition formula:**\n   \\[\n   \\cos(\\alpha + \\beta) = \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\n   \\]\n   Thus,\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = -(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta) = \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta - \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n6. **Express \\(\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\\) in terms of \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = \\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n   Given \\(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n7. **Substitute \\(\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta\\) back into the expression for \\(\\cos \\gamma\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta = \\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} - 1\\right) \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n8. **Calculate the coefficient:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} - 1 = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\cos \\gamma = \\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}\\right) \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta\n   \\]\n\n9. **Determine \\(\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\cos \\gamma} = \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}{\\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}{3}\\right) \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta} = \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3} - 3}\n   \\]\n\n10. **Rationalize the denominator:**\n    \\[\n    \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3} - 3} \\cdot \\frac{2\\sqrt{3} + 3}{2\\sqrt{3} + 3} = \\frac{3(2\\sqrt{3} + 3)}{(2\\sqrt{3})^2 - 3^2} = \\frac{3(2\\sqrt{3} + 3)}{12 - 9} = \\frac{3(2\\sqrt{3} + 3)}{3} = 2\\sqrt{3} + 3\n    \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\sqrt{3} + 3}\n\\]","id":"precalculus:399"}
